          "create_time": 1793549766.687,
          "update_time": 1793549779.206,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The primary sources confirm that low-order coefficient positivity is already known, so another small determinant check would only validate a method. I’ve found a more useful candidate to examine: integration by parts turns the coefficient determinant into a real multiple integral involving even derivatives of the source. This gives the Jacobi identities a concrete place to enter, though the determinant’s sign still needs an argument."
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": false,
          "metadata": {
