          "create_time": 1793549914.805,
          "update_time": 1793549916.466,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The comparison now points toward the determinant route for a limited pilot. Positive averaging alone cannot preserve the Jensen kernels’ real zeros; an exact two-point example shows the failure. For a third-order coefficient determinant, the real integral reduces to the orientation of the curve \\((\\Phi''/\\Phi,\\Phi^{(4)}/\\Phi)\\). Monotonicity and convexity would suffice to sign it, giving us explicit conditions to audit before attempting a broader argument."
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": false,
