          "create_time": 1793550198.967,
          "update_time": 1793550203.011,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Completed the initial comparison and saved the [decision note and follow-up contract](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/07_positive_theta_primitives/jensen/notes/01_J_B01_COEFFICIENT_REPRESENTATION_DECISION_20261101.md).\n\nI recommend **coefficient Toeplitz determinants** for the first pilot. Integration by parts gives an exact real multiple integral whose unresolved sign lies in a determinant of even source derivatives. For order three, a sufficient condition becomes monotonicity and convexity of the curve\n\\[\nu\\longmapsto\\left(\\frac{\\Phi''(u)}{\\Phi(u)},\\frac{\\Phi^{(4)}(u)}{\\Phi(u)}\\right).\n\\]\nThis gives the Jacobi identities a concrete estimating problem.\n\nFor direct Jensen polynomials, I derived the Laguerre-kernel representation and an exact counterexample showing that positive averaging alone does not preserve real roots.\n\n**The required theta curvature signs remain unproved.** Order-three coefficient positivity is already known, so this pilot tests the transfer mechanism rather than extending the established range. [Katkova, Theorem 1](https://arxiv.org/html/math/0505174v1)\n\nThe progress register and reference records are updated. **Next: [E] J-E01 — Sol:** audit the formula and normalization, then check the proposed source conditions at the origin and in the tail before attempting a global argument."
            ]
